      "repairSkill": "tax_incidence_elasticity",
      "commonError": "Assigning economic tax burden by statutory collection rather than relative elasticity.",
      "feedback": "Supply is less elastic than demand, so sellers are less able to adjust quantity and bear the larger share through lower net receipts. Collecting the tax from renters does not make renters bear the larger share. Relative inelasticity does not imply that sellers bear the entire tax.",
