      "q": "A firm produces $1M of output, sells $800,000 to customers, and adds $200,000 to inventory. It pays $600,000 in wages, $100,000 in rent, $100,000 in interest, and has $200,000 in profit. Which statement is correct?",
      "options": [
        "GDP rises by $1M and income generated also totals $1M",
        "GDP rises only by $800,000 because inventories are unsold",
        "GDP rises by $1.2M because inventory is added to sales",
        "GDP rises by wages only"
      ],
      "tag": "gdp_income_expenditure",
      "type": "multi-step",
      "objective": "LO24.1",
      "feedback": "Unsold output is inventory investment, so all $1M counts; income payments also total $1M.",
      "aHash": "22c9e0e01f7c3659fee22f5300f508513c66ffb68e8832ce0446a3e1b017718c",
      "canonicalId": "ECON-NL-ELITE-302",
