      "commonError": "Forgetting that a binding wage floor creates a surplus when labor supplied exceeds labor demanded.",
      "q": "A wage floor is $16. At that wage, 112 workers seek jobs and firms hire 88. A demand increase raises desired hiring to 100 while the wage and labor supply stay fixed. What happens to the labor surplus?",
