      "feedback": "Approximate real growth is 8−5 = 3 percent (the exact ratio gives about 2.9 percent). A lower unemployment rate alone does not prove stronger employment: unemployed workers may have stopped searching. Employment and participation evidence would distinguish the possibilities.",
