      "feedback": "Both initial increases raise quantity, but their opposing price effects need not cancel in general. They happen to cancel at P2 in this drawing. With D2 fixed, partially reversing S2 toward S1 places the new intersection between (P2,Q3) and (P3,Q2). Price rises above P2, and quantity falls from Q3 but remains above Q2 and the original Q1.",
