      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “Employment is unchanged and both rates are unchanged; inactive adults cannot affect the denominator” in this unemployment measurement task.",
      "feedback": "Active searchers without jobs enter both unemployment and the labor force. Employment is unchanged; unemployment rises relative to the larger labor force, and participation rises. A higher unemployment rate need not mean jobs were lost.",
