      "repairSkill": "real_interest_rate_interpretation",
      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “The real repayment is fixed by the nominal contract, so changing inflation changes neither party's position” in this real versus nominal interest rates task.",
      "feedback": "Relative to the forecast, lower inflation makes each repaid dollar more valuable. The nominal obligation does not automatically adjust, so the lender gains and borrower loses relative to expectation.",
      "aHash": "2d2178c504a24411e93231b0ddc9fa48f04afc211dc9010198a63a523b47502c",
