      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “Expected real interest was 2% and realized real interest is 5%; the lender gains relative to expectation” in this real versus nominal interest rates task.",
      "feedback": "The fixed loan has expected real return 8−3=5% but realized return 8−6=2%. A contract that preserves the expected real return would adjust nominal payments for inflation; the fixed borrower therefore benefits relative to that counterfactual.",
