      "repairSkill": "catch_up_growth",
      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “The capital-rich economy must have higher percentage growth because its output level is higher” in this sources of productivity task.",
      "feedback": "Diminishing returns describe the output gain from an additional unit of capital. They do not supply that capital. A binding financing constraint can prevent accumulation despite attractive returns, so conditional catch-up potential is not a prediction of realized convergence.",
