      "feedback": "Nominal GDP becomes $192, and the deflator factor is 0.96. Dividing 192 by 0.96 returns $200 in base prices. Using 1.06 instead would falsely suggest a 9.4% real decline because CPI covers imported food rather than domestic machinery.",
      "aHash": "1539707b9ba73e7078ba8872203c4052b6af84f203cbbf2539a02934a25e2a3c",
